{% doc %}
  Product — the centre of the site, and the only page that consumes the
  full Shopify data layer. Replaces Horizon's `product-information`.

  ── The job ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  CREATIVE-BRIEF.md §03: "prevent the wrong size being ordered." That is
  the literal job, because change-of-mind returns are not accepted. Every
  element here exists to answer a question before it becomes a return
  request, and nothing on this page links away mid-decision (§3.4) —
  claims expand in place.

  ── Composition · "the ledger" ────────────────────────────────────────
  The buy zone is deliberately conventional: a scrolling gallery beside a
  sticky decision column. Tier A (§3.8) allows state changes only — no
  scroll reveals, no 3D, no reveal classes anywhere in this file.

  The brand appears BELOW it, where this brand's argument actually is:
  the ledger. The garment's own measurements in the size guide's
  emerald-head card with the selected row lit; then description, fabric,
  fit and care as accordions (owner's direction, Sep 2026 — replacing
  the three standing columns); the Legal Metrology block stays open as a
  filed record under the design code, because it is a statutory
  disclosure.

  Sep 2026 rebuild, from the owner's reference stores: thumbnail gallery
  with hover zoom (sweetlime), age-stepper sizes with line figures and a
  sizing note (bumchi), an age popup for visitors who did not arrive by
  age (lunabee), an Ask · Save · Share row and promise tiles (lunabee),
  a share menu by the title (mom & zoey), a desktop sticky bar with a
  size select (lemoon). Recommendations, recently viewed, reels and
  reviews are their own sections in templates/product.json.

  ── Must-know is never inside an accordion (HANDOFF rule 6) ───────────
  Always visible: size, the size run, the sizing note, the delivery
  promise (tiles), the returns position, the per-unit price, the
  measurement table. Folded: per-zone delivery charges (the promise is
  already open above it) and the accordions below the fold.

  ── What renders nothing rather than empty (HANDOFF rule 5) ───────────
  Colourway siblings without a group · complete-the-set without
  references · declarations without values · the AI notice when the flag
  is false · reviews, which have no markup here at all until real ones
  exist (ARCHITECTURE §27.2 — no heading, no empty state).
{% enddoc %}

{{ 'sv-product.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'sv-card.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign mf = product.metafields.custom
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign fabric = mf.fabric_composition.value
  assign gsm = mf.fabric_gsm.value
  assign care = mf.care_instructions.value
  assign azo = mf.azo_free.value
  assign shrinkage = mf.shrinkage.value
  assign colourfastness = mf.colourfastness.value
  assign design_code = mf.design_code.value
  assign colourway = mf.colourway.value
  assign colour_group = mf.colour_group.value
  assign pack_size = mf.pack_size.value
  assign ai_imagery = mf.ai_imagery_used.value
  assign size_chart = mf.size_chart.value

  assign whatsapp = shop.metafields.custom.whatsapp_number.value
  assign dispatch = shop.metafields.custom.dispatch_promise.value

  # Per-unit price. DATA-MODEL §3: pack_size drives it, and it is must-know
  # (HANDOFF rule 6), so it sits beside the price and never in a panel.
  assign show_per_unit = false
  if pack_size and pack_size > 1
    assign show_per_unit = true
    assign per_unit = variant.price | divided_by: pack_size
  endif

  # The first line of the care text is the standing Care column; the whole
  # thing is the expander. newline_to_br is the only reliable way to split a
  # multi_line_text_field in Liquid.
  assign care_lines = care | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
  assign care_first = care_lines.first | strip

  assign form_id = 'sv-pdp-form-' | append: section.id
  assign share_url = shop.url | append: product.url

  # Age bands: the popup's choices AND the stepper's full run.
  assign bands = section.settings.age_bands | default: '0–3 m, 3–6 m, 6–9 m, 9–12 m, 12–18 m, 18–24 m, 2–3 y, 3–4 y, 4–5 y, 5–6 y, 6–7 y, 7–8 y' | split: ','
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Product JSON-LD. sv-meta.liquid deliberately does NOT emit this — it
  documents that Horizon's product-information section does, via the
  structured_data filter. This section replaces that one, so the schema
  moves here with it. Losing it would have been silent.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
  {{ product | structured_data }}
</script>

{%- comment -%}
    Each cell's body is built FIRST and the cell is only rendered if
    it came out with something in it.

    §6.8 asks for the three labels in the same order on every product,
    and the first build read that as "always render all three". On a
    product with no fabric and no care text that produced a bare
    FABRIC heading with nothing under it — which ARCHITECTURE rule 11
    forbids outright: an absent field contributes nothing, no label,
    no dash, no placeholder. A label over empty space tells a
    customer nothing and reads as a broken page. Same order, yes;
    same count, no.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture cell_fabric -%}
    {%- capture fabric_line -%}
      {%- if fabric != blank -%}{{ fabric }}~{%- endif -%}
      {%- if gsm != blank -%}{{ gsm }} GSM~{%- endif -%}
      {%- if azo -%}azo-free declared~{%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign fabric_parts = fabric_line | strip | split: '~' -%}
    {%- for part in fabric_parts -%}
      {%- unless forloop.first %} &middot; {% endunless -%}{{ part | strip }}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- capture cell_care -%}{{ care_first }}{%- endcapture -%}

  {%- liquid
    # An expander exists only where its source field does, so the
    # expander rail can be empty on a product that has none.
    assign has_expanders = false
    if gsm != blank or azo or care != blank or shrinkage != blank or colourfastness != blank
      assign has_expanders = true
    endif
  -%}

<section class="sv-pdp" data-sv data-sv-pdp>
  <div class="w sv-pdp__w">
    {%- comment -%}
      Breadcrumb. sv-meta emits BreadcrumbList JSON-LD on this template;
      this is its visible counterpart. `collection` is only set when the
      visitor arrived through one, so the trail never invents a path.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <nav class="sv-pdp__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a>
      {%- if collection -%}
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a href="{{ collection.url }}">{{ collection.title }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">{{ product.title }}</span>
    </nav>

    {%- comment -%} ══ BUY ZONE ══════════════════════════════════════ {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sv-pdp__buy">

      {%- comment -%}
        ── Gallery (Sep 2026 rebuild) ───────────────────────────────
        Thumbnail rail · one stage · arrows, with a hover lens that fills
        a zoom pane over the decision column on desktop (the sweetlime
        pattern). The stage is ONE native scroll-snap row, so a phone
        swipes it with no script and the arrows/thumbs only scroll it.
        The zoom pane reads a 2400px rendition from data-zoom and is
        pointer-only: touch screens pinch natively instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sv-pdp__gallery sv-gal" data-sv-gal>
        {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
          {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
            <ul class="sv-gal__thumbs" role="list">
              {%- for media in product.media -%}
                <li>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="sv-gal__thumb{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}"
                    data-sv-gal-thumb="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                    aria-label="Show {% if media.media_type == 'video' or media.media_type == 'external_video' %}video{% else %}image{% endif %} {{ forloop.index }} of {{ product.media.size }}"
                    {% if forloop.first %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                  >
                    {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 180 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: '', sizes: '90px', widths: '90, 180' }}
                    {%- if media.media_type == 'video' or media.media_type == 'external_video' -%}
                      <span class="sv-gal__play" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M8 5.5v13l11-6.5z"/></svg></span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="sv-gal__stage">
            <ul class="sv-gal__track" role="list" data-sv-gal-track tabindex="0" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} images and videos">
              {%- for media in product.media -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign img = media.preview_image
                  if forloop.first
                    assign frame_loading = 'eager'
                    assign frame_priority = 'high'
                  else
                    assign frame_loading = 'lazy'
                    assign frame_priority = 'auto'
                  endif
                -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Product videos play IN the carousel, in their place in the
                  media order Admin sets — a slide like any photograph, so a
                  swipe, a thumb and the arrows reach it the same way. Muted,
                  looping and inline; sv-product.js plays it only while its
                  slide is the one on screen. A YouTube/Vimeo video added to
                  the product plays in its own player. Hover zoom skips both:
                  the zoom reads an <img>, and a video frame has none.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- case media.media_type -%}
                  {%- when 'video' -%}
                    <li class="sv-gal__slide sv-gal__slide--video" data-sv-gal-slide>
                      <div class="im r-product">
                        {{
                          media
                          | video_tag:
                            image_size: '1400x',
                            muted: true,
                            loop: true,
                            playsinline: true,
                            controls: true,
                            preload: 'metadata',
                            class: 'sv-gal__video',
                            alt: media.alt | default: product.title | escape
                        }}
                      </div>
                    </li>
                  {%- when 'external_video' -%}
                    <li class="sv-gal__slide sv-gal__slide--video" data-sv-gal-slide>
                      <div class="im r-product">
                        {{ media | external_video_url: rel: 0, playsinline: 1 | external_video_tag: class: 'sv-gal__video', loading: 'lazy' }}
                      </div>
                    </li>
                  {%- else -%}
                <li class="sv-gal__slide" data-sv-gal-slide data-zoom="{{ img | image_url: width: 2400 }}">
                  <div class="im r-product">
                    {{
                      img
                      | image_url: width: 1400
                      | image_tag:
                        widths: '480, 640, 900, 1200, 1400',
                        sizes: '(max-width: 880px) 100vw, min(640px, 50vw)',
                        loading: frame_loading,
                        fetchpriority: frame_priority,
                        alt: img.alt | default: product.title | escape
                    }}
                  </div>
                </li>
                {%- endcase -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>

            {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
              <button type="button" class="sv-gal__arrow sv-gal__arrow--prev" data-sv-gal-step="-1" aria-label="Previous image">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m14.5 6-6 6 6 6"/></svg>
              </button>
              <button type="button" class="sv-gal__arrow sv-gal__arrow--next" data-sv-gal-step="1" aria-label="Next image">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m9.5 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg>
              </button>
              <p class="sv-gal__count" aria-hidden="true"><span data-sv-gal-index>1</span> / {{ product.media.size }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            <span class="sv-gal__lens" data-sv-gal-lens hidden></span>
          </div>

          <div class="sv-gal__zoom" data-sv-gal-zoom hidden aria-hidden="true"></div>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            No photography yet. Placeholder fields, no invented caption
            — criterion 5 forbids fabricated content, and a caption
            explaining the absence is content nobody wrote.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The rail stands as empty frames too, so the page keeps the
            shape it will have on the day photography lands. Decorative
            only: nothing to click, nothing announced.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <ul class="sv-gal__thumbs" role="list" aria-hidden="true">
            <li><span class="sv-gal__thumb is-on sv-gal__thumb--ph"><span class="im r-product"></span></span></li>
            <li><span class="sv-gal__thumb sv-gal__thumb--ph"><span class="im im--b r-product"></span></span></li>
            <li><span class="sv-gal__thumb sv-gal__thumb--ph"><span class="im im--c r-product"></span></span></li>
          </ul>
          <div class="sv-gal__stage">
            <ul class="sv-gal__track" role="list">
              <li class="sv-gal__slide"><div class="im r-product" role="img" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} — photography to come"></div></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The AI-imagery notice sits ON the gallery, not in a footnote.
          Terms of Service §3 tells buyers to "rely on the unedited
          photograph and on the size chart", so the disclosure has to be
          where the photographs are. Driven by the metafield, never by
          hand (ARCHITECTURE §6.8 element 12).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if ai_imagery -%}
          <p class="sv-pdp__ai sv-fine">
            Some images on this page are illustrative and computer-generated.
            Every photograph of the garment itself is a real photograph of the
            item you will receive.
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          ── Sizing note (the bumchi box) ───────────────────────
          Must-know, so it stands open. Sits under the gallery and its
          AI notice (owner's direction, Sep 2026), not in the column. Two routes out of doubt: the measurements on this
          page (a same-page jump, §3.4), or a person on WhatsApp.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sv-pdp__sizenote">
          <p>
            <strong>Note:</strong> sizes vary by brand.
            {%- if size_chart != blank %} Check
              <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__notelink" data-sv-chart-open aria-haspopup="dialog">this garment&rsquo;s size chart</button>
              for the right fit &mdash;
            {%- else %} For the right fit,
            {%- endif %} measure a garment your child already wears, laid flat.
          </p>
          {%- if whatsapp != blank -%}
            <p>Not sure, or missing a measurement? <a href="https://wa.me/{{ whatsapp }}?text={{ 'Hi, can you help me pick a size for ' | append: product.title | append: '? ' | append: share_url | url_encode | replace: '+', '%20' }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-sv-wa-size>WhatsApp us</a></p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          ── Details · Fabric · Care (Sep 2026) ──
          Expandable, under the photographs and the sizing note (owner's
          direction): the left column ran short of the buy column, so the
          details fill that space and "You may also like" still follows
          straight on after the product. Size guide and Fit were removed
          — the "Size chart" link by the price and the sizing note above
          already open the chart. Details opens by default.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sv-acc sv-pdp__acc">

        {%- if product.description != blank -%}
          <details class="sv-acc__item" open>
            <summary>Details</summary>
            <div class="sv-acc__body sv-pdp__rte">{{ product.description }}</div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}


        {%- if cell_fabric != blank or gsm != blank or azo or shrinkage != blank or colourfastness != blank -%}
          <details class="sv-acc__item">
            <summary>Fabric</summary>
            <div class="sv-acc__body">
              {%- if cell_fabric != blank -%}<p>{{ cell_fabric | strip }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if gsm != blank -%}
                <p>
                  <strong>What {{ gsm }} GSM means.</strong> GSM is grams per square metre &mdash;
                  the weight of the fabric. {{ gsm }} is a mid-weight knit: substantial enough to
                  hold its shape after washing, light enough for Kerala heat. Thin kidswear is
                  often 120&ndash;140, which is why it goes shapeless after a few washes.
                </p>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if azo -%}
                <p>
                  <strong>Azo-free.</strong> 112 azo dyes are prohibited in textiles under
                  India&rsquo;s Environment (Protection) Act because they can release compounds
                  that irritate skin. Our supplier provides a signed declaration for every batch.
                  This is a legal standard, not a marketing claim.
                </p>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if shrinkage != blank or colourfastness != blank -%}
                <dl class="sv-pdp__dl">
                  {%- if shrinkage != blank -%}<dt>Shrinkage</dt><dd>{{ shrinkage }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if colourfastness != blank -%}<dt>Colourfastness</dt><dd>{{ colourfastness }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                </dl>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}


        {%- if care != blank -%}
          <details class="sv-acc__item">
            <summary>Care guide</summary>
            <div class="sv-acc__body"><p>{{ care | newline_to_br }}</p></div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        ── Decision column ──────────────────────────────────────────
        Sticky on desktop. Element order follows ARCHITECTURE §6.8
        exactly: title · price · per-unit · size · size run · design
        code · add to cart · sizing · delivery · returns.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sv-pdp__col">
        <div class="sv-pdp__stick">

          {%- comment -%}
            ── Colourway siblings ─────────────────────────────────
            DATA-MODEL §5. The `group:` TAG is the query mechanism, not
            the metafield — the metafield drives display only, and where
            the two disagree the tag wins. Never iterate
            collections.all.products unfiltered.

            Ceiling worth knowing: collections.all.products yields at
            most 50 products to Liquid without paginate, so a colour
            group whose members sit beyond the first 50 of the catalogue
            would not be found. Correct at this catalogue size; the scale
            answer is a per-group collection, not a bigger loop here.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if colour_group != blank -%}
            {%- assign group_tag = 'group:' | append: colour_group -%}
            {%- assign siblings = collections.all.products | where: 'tags', group_tag -%}
            {%- if siblings.size > 1 -%}
              <div class="sv-pdp__colours">
                <span class="lab lab--grey">More colours</span>
                <ul class="sv-pdp__swatches" role="list">
                  {%- for sibling in siblings -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign s_name = sibling.metafields.custom.colourway.value | default: sibling.title
                      assign s_hex = sibling.metafields.custom.colour_swatch.value
                      assign is_current = false
                      if sibling.handle == product.handle
                        assign is_current = true
                      endif
                    -%}
                    <li>
                      <a
                        class="sv-pdp__swatch{% if is_current %} is-current{% endif %}{% unless sibling.available %} is-out{% endunless %}"
                        href="{{ sibling.url }}"
                        {% if is_current %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                      >
                        <span class="sv-pdp__dot" style="--sv-swatch: {{ s_hex | default: '#E9E1CD' }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        {%- comment -%}
                          A sibling sold out in every size is struck
                          through and STILL LINKED (DATA-MODEL §5) — it is
                          a real design, and hiding it makes the range
                          look thinner than it is.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        <span class="sv-pdp__swatchname">
                          {{- s_name }}{% unless sibling.available %} &mdash; sold out{% endunless -%}
                        </span>
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="sv-pdp__titlerow">
            <h1 class="sv-pdp__title">{{ product.title }}</h1>
            <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__iconbtn" data-sv-share-open aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="Share this product">
              {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'share' %}
            </button>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Stars under the title (momandzoey): Judge.me's preview badge,
            linking down to the reviews. Judge.me fills it in and leaves
            it blank on a product with no reviews, so nothing shows until
            there is something true to show.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if product.metafields.judgeme != blank or shop.metafields.judgeme != blank -%}
            <a class="sv-pdp__rating" href="#reviews">
              <span class="jdgm-widget jdgm-preview-badge" data-id="{{ product.id }}">{{ product.metafields.judgeme.badge }}</span>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Share menu. One panel, opened from the title icon and from the
            action row. On a phone the script hands off to the native share
            sheet (navigator.share) and this panel never opens; on desktop,
            where that sheet is patchy, these links are the menu. Every link
            works without script.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="sv-share" data-sv-share hidden role="dialog" aria-label="Share this product">
            <p class="lab lab--grey sv-share__lab">Share</p>
            <ul class="sv-share__list" role="list">
              <li><a class="sv-share__link" data-sv-share-link="whatsapp" href="https://wa.me/?text={{ product.title | append: ' ' | append: share_url | url_encode | replace: '+', '%20' }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'whatsapp' %}<span>WhatsApp</span></a></li>
              <li><a class="sv-share__link" data-sv-share-link="facebook" href="https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u={{ share_url | url_encode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'facebook' %}<span>Facebook</span></a></li>
              <li><a class="sv-share__link" data-sv-share-link="pinterest" href="https://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url={{ share_url | url_encode }}{% if product.featured_image %}&media={{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' | url_encode }}{% endif %}&description={{ product.title | url_encode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'pinterest' %}<span>Pinterest</span></a></li>
              <li><a class="sv-share__link" data-sv-share-link="email" href="mailto:?subject={{ product.title | url_encode }}&body={{ share_url | url_encode }}">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'mail' %}<span>Email</span></a></li>
              <li><button type="button" class="sv-share__link" data-sv-share-copy data-url="{{ share_url }}">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'link' %}<span data-sv-share-copy-label>Copy link</span></button></li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Price on the left; stock, size chart and the remembered age
            beside it on the right (owner's direction, Sep 2026) — one
            row instead of three stacked lines.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="sv-pdp__pricerow">
          <div class="sv-pdp__pricing">
            <p class="sv-pdp__price" data-sv-price>
              {{- variant.price | money -}}
              {%- if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price -%}
                <s class="sv-pdp__was">{{ variant.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
              {%- endif -%}
            </p>

            {%- if show_per_unit -%}
              <p class="sv-pdp__unit">{{ per_unit | money }} each &middot; pack of {{ pack_size }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price -%}
              {%- assign saving = variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price -%}
              <p class="sv-pdp__saving">You save {{ saving | money }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
            <div class="sv-pdp__meta">
              {%- render 'sv-size-run', product: product, class: 'sv-pdp__run' -%}
              {%- if size_chart != blank -%}
                <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__chartlink" data-sv-chart-open aria-haspopup="dialog">Size chart</button>
              {%- endif -%}
                  <p class="sv-pdp__agenow sv-fine" data-sv-age-now hidden>
                    Shopping for <strong data-sv-age-now-label></strong>
                    &middot; <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__agechange" data-sv-age-open>change</button>
                  </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <form
            id="{{ form_id }}"
            class="sv-pdp__form"
            action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
            method="post"
            enctype="multipart/form-data"
            data-sv-pdp-form
            data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
          >
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ variant.id }}" data-sv-variant-input>

            {%- comment -%}
              ── Size, as buttons ───────────────────────────────────
              Never a dropdown: Baymard found 57% of sites use one, and
              a dropdown hides availability behind a tap. Sold-out sizes
              are struck through and stay VISIBLE — a size that is
              missing from the page reads as a size that was never made.

              Buttons iterate variants rather than option values, so
              availability is exact per button with no lookup, and the
              markup survives a product that ever gains a second option.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              ── Size, as an age stepper (Sep 2026) ─────────────────
              Still buttons, never a dropdown, and sold-out sizes stay
              visible and selectable. Each stop carries a line figure
              for its age stage (the bumchi pattern) so a parent reads
              "crawling" before they read "9–12 m".

              data-from / data-to are the size's age range in MONTHS,
              parsed here once from the variant title, so the age picker
              can match "6–9 m" to a variant cut "6-12m" without the
              script re-parsing strings.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
              <fieldset class="sv-pdp__sizes">
                <legend class="lab lab--grey sv-pdp__sizelab">Size <span class="sv-pdp__sizehint">(select age)</span></legend>


                {%- comment -%}
                  By default the stepper lists exactly the product's own
                  sizes (owner's direction, Sep 2026). The "group" and "all"
                  settings widen it to the age scale, with the bands the
                  design is NOT made in greyed. Where one of the
                  design's own sizes spans several bands ("0-6m" over 0–3
                  and 3–6), the size replaces them — never a stop twice.

                  Entries are built as "MMM|kind|ref" strings, zero-padded
                  on the start month, so a plain `sort` orders bands and
                  sizes together.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign step_mode = section.settings.step_run | default: 'own'
                  assign v_ranges = ''
                  assign groups = ','
                  assign entries = ''
                  for v in product.variants
                    capture r
                      render 'sv-age-range', label: v.title
                    endcapture
                    assign r = r | split: ','
                    assign vf = r.first | plus: 0
                    assign vt = r.last | plus: 0
                    assign v_ranges = v_ranges | append: vf | append: '-' | append: vt | append: ';'
                    if vf < 12
                      assign g = '0'
                    elsif vf < 36
                      assign g = '1'
                    elsif vf < 72
                      assign g = '2'
                    else
                      assign g = '3'
                    endif
                    assign groups = groups | append: g | append: ','
                    assign pad = vf | prepend: '00'
                    assign pad = pad | slice: -3, 3
                    assign entries = entries | append: pad | append: '|v|' | append: forloop.index0 | append: '~'
                  endfor

                  if step_mode != 'own'
                    for band in bands
                      assign b = band | strip
                      if b == blank
                        continue
                      endif
                      capture r
                        render 'sv-age-range', label: b
                      endcapture
                      assign r = r | split: ','
                      assign bf = r.first | plus: 0
                      assign bt = r.last | plus: 0
                      if bf < 12
                        assign g = ',0,'
                      elsif bf < 36
                        assign g = ',1,'
                      elsif bf < 72
                        assign g = ',2,'
                      else
                        assign g = ',3,'
                      endif
                      if step_mode == 'group'
                        unless groups contains g
                          continue
                        endunless
                      endif
                      assign covered = false
                      assign vr_list = v_ranges | split: ';'
                      for vr in vr_list
                        assign vr_parts = vr | split: '-'
                        assign xf = vr_parts.first | plus: 0
                        assign xt = vr_parts.last | plus: 0
                        if xf < bt and bf < xt
                          assign covered = true
                          break
                        endif
                      endfor
                      if covered
                        continue
                      endif
                      assign pad = bf | prepend: '00'
                      assign pad = pad | slice: -3, 3
                      assign entries = entries | append: pad | append: '|b|' | append: b | append: '~'
                    endfor
                  endif

                  assign entries = entries | split: '~' | sort
                  assign has_ghost = false
                  if entries.size > product.variants.size
                    assign has_ghost = true
                  endif
                -%}
                <div class="sv-step" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Size" data-sv-step>
                  {%- for entry in entries -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign parts = entry | split: '|'
                      assign start_m = parts[0] | plus: 0
                      if start_m < 3
                        assign stage = 'newborn'
                      elsif start_m < 6
                        assign stage = 'swaddle'
                      elsif start_m < 9
                        assign stage = 'sit'
                      elsif start_m < 12
                        assign stage = 'crawl'
                      elsif start_m < 18
                        assign stage = 'toddle'
                      elsif start_m < 24
                        assign stage = 'toddle2'
                      elsif start_m < 36
                        assign stage = 'twos'
                      elsif start_m < 48
                        assign stage = 'walk'
                      elsif start_m < 72
                        assign stage = 'kid'
                      else
                        assign stage = 'big'
                      endif
                    -%}
                    {%- if parts[1] == 'b' -%}
                      {%- comment -%} A band this design is not made in: shown, never selectable. {%- endcomment -%}
                      <span class="sv-step__opt is-none" title="Not made in {{ parts[2] | escape }}">
                        <span class="sv-step__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="sv-step__label">{{ parts[2] }}<span class="sv-visually-hidden"> — not made in this design</span></span>
                        {% render 'sv-baby', stage: stage, class: 'sv-step__baby' %}
                      </span>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- liquid
                        assign vi = parts[2] | plus: 0
                        assign v = product.variants[vi]
                        capture r
                          render 'sv-age-range', label: v.title
                        endcapture
                        assign r = r | split: ','
                      -%}
                      <button
                        type="button"
                        class="sv-step__opt sv-pdp__size{% if v.id == variant.id %} is-on{% endif %}{% unless v.available %} is-out{% endunless %}"
                        role="radio"
                        aria-checked="{% if v.id == variant.id %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                        data-sv-size
                        data-variant-id="{{ v.id }}"
                        data-available="{{ v.available }}"
                        data-stock="{% if v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy == 'deny' %}{{ v.inventory_quantity | at_least: 0 }}{% endif %}"
                        data-price="{{ v.price | money }}"
                        data-compare="{% if v.compare_at_price > v.price %}{{ v.compare_at_price | money }}{% endif %}"
                        data-title="{{ v.title | escape }}"
                        data-label="{{ v.title | replace: '-', '–' | escape }}"
                        data-from="{{ r.first }}"
                        data-to="{{ r.last }}"
                        {% unless v.available %}aria-describedby="{{ form_id }}-out"{% endunless %}
                      >
                        <span class="sv-step__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="sv-step__label">{{ v.title | replace: '-', '–' }}</span>
                        {% render 'sv-baby', stage: stage, class: 'sv-step__baby' %}
                        {%- unless v.available -%}<span class="sv-step__tag" aria-hidden="true">sold out</span>{%- endunless -%}
                      </button>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
                {%- comment -%}
                  Two different "no"s, said differently: a band the design is
                  never made in (greyed, dashed) and a size that exists but is
                  sold out right now (crossed out, still selectable). The note
                  names only the cases this product actually has.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign has_soldout = false
                  for v in product.variants
                    unless v.available
                      assign has_soldout = true
                      break
                    endunless
                  endfor
                -%}
                {%- if has_ghost or has_soldout -%}
                  <p class="sv-step__legend sv-fine">
                    {%- if has_ghost -%}<span class="sv-step__key sv-step__key--none">Greyed: not made in this design</span>{%- endif -%}
                    {%- if has_ghost and has_soldout -%}<span aria-hidden="true"> &middot; </span>{%- endif -%}
                    {%- if has_soldout -%}<span class="sv-step__key sv-step__key--out">Crossed out: sold out right now</span>{%- endif -%}
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span id="{{ form_id }}-out" class="sv-visually-hidden">sold out</span>
              </fieldset>
            {%- endunless -%}

            <div class="sv-pdp__actions">
              <div class="sv-pdp__qty">
                <label class="sv-visually-hidden" for="{{ form_id }}-qty">Quantity</label>
                <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__qtybtn" data-sv-qty="-1" aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
                <input
                  id="{{ form_id }}-qty"
                  class="sv-pdp__qtyinput"
                  type="number"
                  name="quantity"
                  value="1"
                  min="1"
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Stock cap for the size selected on load: the browser
                    enforces it without JS, and sv-product.js reads
                    data-stock when there is no size stepper (one-size
                    designs). Blank means Shopify is not limiting stock.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- if variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' and variant.inventory_policy == 'deny' and variant.inventory_quantity > 0 %}
                    max="{{ variant.inventory_quantity }}"
                    data-stock="{{ variant.inventory_quantity }}"
                  {%- endif %}
                  step="1"
                  inputmode="numeric"
                  data-sv-qty-input
                >
                <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__qtybtn" data-sv-qty="1" aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
              </div>

              <button
                type="submit"
                class="btn sv-pdp__add"
                data-sv-add
                {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
              >
                <span data-sv-add-label>
                  {%- if variant.available -%}Add to bag{%- else -%}Sold out{%- endif -%}
                </span>
              </button>
            </div>

            <p class="sv-pdp__formerr sv-fine" data-sv-error hidden role="status"></p>
          </form>

          {%- if design_code != blank -%}
            <p class="sv-pdp__code sv-fine sv-fine--caps">Design {{ design_code }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            ── The three must-know facts ──────────────────────────
            Sizing, delivery, returns. ARCHITECTURE §6.8 elements 7, 8
            and 9, and HANDOFF rule 6 forbids any of the three from
            sitting inside a closed panel. They are plain paragraphs
            here for exactly that reason.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            ── Ask · Save · Share (the lunabee row) ────────────────
            ARCHITECTURE §6.8 element 13 moved up beside Save and Share.
            The WhatsApp prefill now carries the PAGE LINK as well as the
            product and selected size, so the reply starts from the right
            garment even when the message is forwarded; the script keeps
            the size and the ?variant in step with the selection.

            Save is a device-local wishlist (localStorage `sv_saved`,
            product handles). No account needed, nothing sent anywhere.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="sv-pdp__row">
            {%- if whatsapp != blank -%}
              {%- capture wa_text -%}Hi, I'd like to ask about {{ product.title }} ({{ variant.title }}){% if design_code != blank %}, design {{ design_code }}{% endif %}. {{ share_url }}?variant={{ variant.id }}{%- endcapture -%}
              <a
                class="sv-pdp__rowbtn sv-pdp__rowbtn--wa"
                href="https://wa.me/{{ whatsapp }}?text={{ wa_text | url_encode | replace: '+', '%20' }}"
                rel="noopener"
                target="_blank"
                data-sv-wa
                data-wa-base="https://wa.me/{{ whatsapp }}?text="
                data-wa-product="{{ product.title | escape }}"
                data-wa-code="{{ design_code | escape }}"
                data-wa-url="{{ share_url }}"
              >{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'whatsapp' %}<span>Ask us on WhatsApp</span></a>
            {%- endif -%}
            <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__rowbtn" data-sv-save data-handle="{{ product.handle }}" aria-pressed="false">
              {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'heart' %}<span data-sv-save-label>Wishlist</span>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="sv-pdp__rowbtn" data-sv-share-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
              {% render 'sv-icon', name: 'share' %}<span>Share</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            ── Promise tiles ──────────────────────────────────────
            Three short facts, each from the store's own data and each
            true today. No "hygiene checked" style claim appears here
            unless it is a process that actually happens.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign threshold = shop.metafields.custom.free_shipping_threshold.value -%}
          <ul class="sv-pdp__tiles" role="list">
            {%- if threshold != blank -%}
              <li class="sv-pdp__tile">
                <span class="sv-pdp__tileicon">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'truck' %}</span>
                <span><strong>Free delivery</strong> on orders over {{ threshold | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if dispatch != blank -%}
              <li class="sv-pdp__tile">
                <span class="sv-pdp__tileicon">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'clock' %}</span>
                <span><strong>{{ dispatch }}</strong> of payment, from Thiruvananthapuram to every pincode</span>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
            <li class="sv-pdp__tile">
              <span class="sv-pdp__tileicon">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'shield' %}</span>
              <span><strong>Damaged or wrong item?</strong> Replaced or refunded in full, postage on us</span>
            </li>
          </ul>



        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    ── Sticky bar, mobile ──────────────────────────────────────────
    §6.8 element 6. Outside the form and bound to it by the `form`
    attribute, so there is one form and one source of truth for the
    selected variant — never a duplicated mobile DOM.

    Hidden until the real Add button scrolls out of view; the observer
    lives in sv-product.js and is an IntersectionObserver, not a scroll
    listener.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if size_chart != blank -%}
    <dialog class="sv-chart" data-sv-chart aria-label="Size chart">
      <form method="dialog" class="sv-chart__panel">
        <button type="submit" class="sv-chart__x" aria-label="Close">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'close' %}</button>
        {{
          size_chart
          | image_url: width: 1400
          | image_tag:
            widths: '720, 1024, 1400',
            sizes: '(max-width: 760px) 94vw, 640px',
            loading: 'lazy',
            alt: size_chart.alt | default: 'Size chart' | escape
        }}
      </form>
    </dialog>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    ── Age picker (the lunabee popup, adapted) ───────────────────────
    Opens once for a visitor who lands on a product WITHOUT having
    chosen an age — not arriving from an age collection, no ?variant in
    the link, and nothing stored yet. The choice is kept on the device
    (localStorage `sv_age`) and pre-selects the matching size on every
    product after, where a "Shopping for … · change" line reopens it.

    Single choice, unlike lunabee's multi-select: on a product page one
    child is being dressed at a time, and one answer maps to one size.
    Bands come from the section setting so they can follow the menu.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.age_popup and product.has_only_default_variant == false -%}
    <dialog class="sv-agepick" data-sv-age data-skip-collections="{{ section.settings.age_collections | escape }}" aria-labelledby="sv-age-h-{{ section.id }}">
      <form method="dialog" class="sv-agepick__panel">
        <h2 class="sv-agepick__h" id="sv-age-h-{{ section.id }}">What size are you shopping for?</h2>
        <p class="sv-agepick__sub">Pick your child&rsquo;s age &mdash; we&rsquo;ll pre-select the right size on every design.</p>
        <div class="sv-agepick__chips" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Age">
          {%- for band in bands -%}
            {%- assign b = band | strip -%}
            {%- if b == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            <button type="button" class="sv-agepick__chip" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-sv-age-band="{{ b | escape }}">{{ b }}</button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        <div class="sv-agepick__actions">
          <button type="button" class="btn sv-agepick__ok" data-sv-age-ok disabled>Show my size</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost sv-agepick__all" data-sv-age-all>Show all sizes</button>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="sv-agepick__x" data-sv-age-all aria-label="Close">{% render 'sv-icon', name: 'close' %}</button>
      </form>
    </dialog>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="sv-pdp__bar" data-sv-bar hidden>
    {%- if product.featured_image -%}
      <span class="sv-pdp__barthumb">{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 120 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: '', widths: '60, 120', sizes: '56px' }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="sv-pdp__barinfo">
      <span class="sv-pdp__barname">{{ product.title }}</span>
      <span class="sv-pdp__barprice" data-sv-bar-price>{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%}
      Desktop only: a size select that drives the SAME size buttons (the
      script calls their select()), so the form keeps one source of truth.
      The stepper stays the primary control; this is a convenience once
      it has scrolled away.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
      <label class="sv-visually-hidden" for="{{ form_id }}-barsize">Size</label>
      <select id="{{ form_id }}-barsize" class="sv-pdp__barsize" data-sv-bar-size>
        {%- for v in product.variants -%}
          <option value="{{ v.id }}" {% if v.id == variant.id %}selected{% endif %}>{{ v.title | replace: '-', '–' }}{% unless v.available %} — sold out{% endunless %}</option>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </select>
    {%- endunless -%}
    <button
      type="submit"
      form="{{ form_id }}"
      class="btn sv-pdp__baradd"
      data-sv-bar-add
      {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
    >
      <span data-sv-bar-label>{% if variant.available %}Add to bag{% else %}Sold out{% endif %}</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{ 'sv-product.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Product",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "sv-pdp-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "step_run",
      "label": "Size stepper shows",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "own",
          "label": "Only this design's sizes"
        },
        {
          "value": "group",
          "label": "Whole age group, others greyed"
        },
        {
          "value": "all",
          "label": "Every age band, others greyed"
        }
      ],
      "default": "own",
      "info": "Default lists exactly the sizes added to each product. The other two also show ages the design isn't made in, greyed."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Age picker popup"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "age_popup",
      "label": "Ask for the child's age on first visit",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "age_bands",
      "label": "Age choices",
      "info": "Comma-separated, e.g. 0–3 m, 3–6 m, 2–3 y. Use m for months and y for years.",
      "default": "0–3 m, 3–6 m, 6–9 m, 9–12 m, 12–18 m, 18–24 m, 2–3 y, 3–4 y, 4–5 y, 5–6 y, 6–7 y, 7–8 y"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "age_collections",
      "label": "Age collections (no popup when arriving from these)",
      "info": "Collection handles, comma-separated.",
      "default": "newborn-0-12-months,toddler-1-3-years,kids-3-6-years,big-kids-6-8-years"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "SV Product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
